.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH xil-parsed-csv 1  "xil-parsed-csv " 
.SH NAME
xil\-parsed\-csv \- Export parsed_<tag>.json entries to CSV — one row per entry
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBxil\-parsed\-csv\fR [\fB\-o\fR|\fB\-\-output\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIPATH\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Export parsed_<tag>.json entries to CSV — one row per entry
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Write CSV to FILE (default: stdout)
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output a JSON array to stdout — no banner, safe to pipe to jq
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
[\fIPATH\fR] [default: __parsed_default__]
parsed JSON file, or directory containing parsed_*.json files (default: workspace parsed/)
